From: opendrop-rs hacking session
Subject: [PATCH] rtw88: suppress TX-status reports for monitor-injected frames

Frames injected through a monitor interface (e.g. by the AWDL daemon `owl`)
carry IEEE80211_TX_CTL_REQ_TX_STATUS. rtw88 then sets the SPE_RPT descriptor
bit, asking the firmware for a per-frame CCX TX report, and queues the skb on
tx_report->queue waiting for it. In monitor mode that report never comes back,
so the 500ms purge timer fires "failed to get tx report from firmware". Under a
high injection rate (owl emits PSF/MIF + data every few TU) this floods the
firmware's report path; on RTL8822BU the USB device then wedges and disconnects
off the bus (cf. lwfinger/rtw88 #368).

Clear REQ_TX_STATUS for vif-less (injected) and monitor frames before the
report-enable check. This stops both the SPE_RPT descriptor bit (tx.c) and the
usb.c enqueue/purge path, since both gate on the same flag.

Result on an RTL8822BU clone running owl: zero "failed to get tx report"
messages and no USB disconnect across 3+ minutes (previously crashed in ~1-2m).

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/tx.c
@@ -419,6 +419,17 @@
 	bmc = is_broadcast_ether_addr(hdr->addr1) ||
 	      is_multicast_ether_addr(hdr->addr1);

+	/* AWDL/owl monitor-injection fix: frames injected through a monitor
+	 * interface have no associated vif here. Requesting per-frame TX status
+	 * reports for them sets the SPE_RPT descriptor bit and queues the skb for
+	 * a firmware CCX report that never arrives in monitor mode. Under owl's
+	 * high injection rate this floods the firmware ("failed to get tx report
+	 * from firmware") and the 8822BU USB device eventually wedges/disconnects.
+	 * Clear the request for vif-less (injected) and monitor frames so neither
+	 * the SPE_RPT bit (below) nor the usb.c tx-report purge path is armed. */
+	if (!vif || vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR)
+		info->flags &= ~IEEE80211_TX_CTL_REQ_TX_STATUS;
+
 	if (info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_REQ_TX_STATUS)
 		rtw_tx_report_enable(rtwdev, pkt_info);

